  "reason": "Evidence: config_012 (avgpool, weighted) achieved 0.635 accuracy, significantly outperforming config_015 (transformer, weighted) at 0.586, establishing avgpool as the superior aggregation. Both used weighted fusion, so the fusion strategy (weighted vs concat) remains untested. Question: config_004 is identical to our best (config_012) except fusion changes from weighted to concat, isolating the effect of fusion strategy while holding the proven avgpool aggregation, pca_n2000 RNA encoder, and imagenet_vit_l image encoder constant. Why: This is the cleanest single-variable exploitation of our current best result. Fusion strategy is a fundamental architectural choice that could meaningfully shift accuracy, and resolving it early (with 7 experiments left) lets us lock in the better fusion for all subsequent exploration of RNA encoders (scvi_n200, scgpt), image encoders (resnet50), and profile settings. Testing concat now maximizes information gain per experiment."
}

